{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I clothe the heavens with darkness.</b> The garment of darkness — the meaning is upon the clouds. Some say: upon the darkening of the sun when it is entirely dark at midday, and it is as though sackcloth covers them, because sackcloth is black."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:51.836658365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}